# Cloud Build source upload filter for the builds that compile the web
# frontend into the scion binary: the omni target (cloudbuild-omni.yaml) and
# the hub-gke stage of the repo-root Dockerfile (cloudbuild-hub-gke.yaml).
#
# The default .gcloudignore excludes web source files (web/*.json,
# web/src/, etc.) because existing Cloud Build configs only compile Go
# with -tags no_embed_web. The omni Dockerfile rebuilds scion WITHOUT
# that tag, running `npm install && npm run build` to embed the web
# frontend. Without this file, the omni build fails at step 8 with
# "ENOENT: no such file or directory, open '/src/web/package.json'".
# The root Dockerfile's frontend stage (used by hub-gke) likewise runs
# `npm ci && npm run build`.
#
# Usage: pass --ignore-file=image-build/gcloudignore-omni to
# gcloud builds submit when building the omni or hub-gke target.
#
# Gitignore semantics: a pattern without a slash matches at any depth, which
# would also drop files under //go:embed roots (e.g. pkg/config/embeds/,
# resources/templates/, harnesses/) from the upload: the build still passes,
# but the files are missing from the binary. So every pattern that names a
# repo-root path is anchored with a leading "/" (patterns with an inner slash,
# such as web/dist/, are already anchored). The few patterns left unanchored
# on purpose say why. cmd/gcloudignore_contract_test.go checks that no tracked
# file under a //go:embed root is matched by any Cloud Build ignore file.

#!include:.gitignore
# (gcloud resolves this next to this file: image-build/.gitignore, not the
# root .gitignore.)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Directories not needed by omni or hub-gke builds
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/changelog/
/docs/
/docs-repo/
/docs-site/
/examples/
/extras/
/hack/
/internal/
/reviews/
/scratch/
/scripts/
/shared-dirs/
/skills/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web frontend — INCLUDE source for omni and hub-gke (unlike .gcloudignore).
# Only exclude build artifacts and tooling detritus.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
web/node_modules/
web/coverage/
web/.screenshots/
web/.env*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test files — Cloud Build compiles Go but never runs tests
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unanchored on purpose: Go tests sit next to the code in every package.
*_test.go

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build artifacts and tool state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .git/, testdata/ and downloads/ are unanchored on purpose:
#   .git/      - VCS metadata of any nested checkout is never build input.
#   testdata/  - Go test fixtures live next to each package (pkg/*/testdata)
#                and Cloud Build does not run tests.
#   downloads/ - agent/harness runtime downloads can land in any directory
#                (mirrors the any-depth downloads/ in .gitignore).
# Everything else here names a repo-root path and is anchored with "/".
.git/
/.claude/
/.design/
/.scratch/
/.tasks/
/.scion/
/build/
/.build/
testdata/
downloads/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI / IDE / config files not needed for image builds
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.gemini/
/.geminiignore
/.github/
/.gitignore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root files not needed for image builds
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/claude.md
/gemini.md
/.claudeignore
/.dockerignore
/.coordinator-state.md
/.eng-manager-state.md
/agents.md
/CHANGELOG.md
/GLOSSARY.md
/LICENSE
/Makefile
/README.md
/pr-*-review*.md
